1
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:16,359
So what's new, Mark? How is your new job

2
00:00:16,859 --> 00:00:20,640
going? To be honest, I can't complain.

3
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:24,720
I really love the company that I am working for.

4
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:29,850
My co workers are all really friendly and helpful.

5
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:32,970
They really help me feel welcome.

6
00:00:34,010 --> 00:00:37,210
It's a really energetic and fun atmosphere.

7
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:42,730
My boss is hilarious and he's really flexible.

8
00:00:43,690 --> 00:00:46,490
Really? How so?

9
00:00:47,610 --> 00:00:51,660
He allows me to come in when I want and make

10
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:56,100
my own hours. I can also leave early if I

11
00:00:56,600 --> 00:01:00,260
start early. There is no real dress code either.

12
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:04,020
I can wear jeans and a T shirt if I want.

13
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:07,620
I can even wear shorts in the summer.

14
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:11,540
Wow, it sounds really cool.

15
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:15,860
I can't stand wearing a suit every day.

16
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:20,550
Which do you prefer? Working late or finishing

17
00:01:21,050 --> 00:01:23,710
early? I prefer finishing early.

18
00:01:24,670 --> 00:01:28,470
I really enjoy the morning. I love getting

19
00:01:28,970 --> 00:01:30,670
up early and going for a run.

20
00:01:31,630 --> 00:01:35,070
There's nothing like watching the sunrise while drinking

21
00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:38,110
my morning coffee. Really?

22
00:01:39,390 --> 00:01:43,150
I am opposite. I love sleeping

23
00:01:43,650 --> 00:01:47,310
in. I am most alert in the evenings.

24
00:01:48,030 --> 00:01:50,030
I'm a real night owl.

25
00:01:54,270 --> 00:01:58,230
Well, you know what they say. The early bird

26
00:01:58,730 --> 00:02:01,870
catches the worm. You know, you could be right.

27
00:02:02,990 --> 00:02:06,430
Maybe I will try to go to bed a little earlier

28
00:02:06,590 --> 00:02:07,230
tonight.

